{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/218912-brainstorm-azothic-radiance","id":218912,"title":"Brainstorm: Azothic Radiance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-05T01:31:38-07:00","id":218912,"title":"Brainstorm: Azothic Radiance","content":"Vampires, werewolves, and mages are picking up various &quot;aura&quot; effects in the post-GMC world. Prometheans will likely follow, should they get updated material, and the Radiance is a pre-existing candidate.<br /> What it does already:<ul><li>&quot;Pings&quot; other Prometheans</li> <li>Awakens Pandorans</li> <li>Gets tracked by Pandorans</li> <li>Can be subdued to avoid tracking</li> <li>Puts other Created at unease when subdued</li> </ul>What it is implicitly affecting:<ul><li>Disquiet</li> <li>Wasteland</li> <li>Spreads Torment</li> </ul>Here comes the brainstorming part. Very few of the above translate to a direct benefit (i.e., a reason to &quot;lash out&quot; a la Predatory Aura). Given its possible ties to Disquiet, it seems tempting to assign it some sort of risky social benefit, like &quot;lashing out&quot; to make a good impression, but this seems counter-thematic. Some alternate ideas:<ul><li>The Promethean can &quot;flare up&quot; to gain a free use of Transhuman Potential once per scene.</li> <li>The Promethean can &quot;flare up&quot; when around mortals to gain an Azoth roll's worth of Pyros rather than the single point, with the roll to resist Disquiet automatically failed.</li> <li>The Promethean can &quot;flare up&quot; to inflict Lineage-inspired Conditions. For example, a Muse might inflict the Wanton Condition.</li> <li>The Promethean can &quot;flare up&quot; to inflict Refinement-inspired Conditions. For example, a Cuprum might drive someone into a fit of navel-gazing or obliviousness.</li> <li>The Promethean can &quot;flare up&quot; to create a short-lived Azothic wonder. Maybe he calls lightning to strike, or flames surge, or electricity arcs from a nearby outlet to heal him.</li> </ul>I also like the idea of a flare being necessary to using more vulgar or aggressive Transmutations. Deception powers rarely ever require a flare, but Vitality leaves the air electric, stirs the Mockeries, and deepens the mortal divide. Or, maybe it's necessary to harness Electroshock Therapy, and if you fall unexpectedly on a live wire, you convulse and burn as any human would.<br /> <br /> Anyway, just getting these out of my head before bedtime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T18:04:32-07:00","id":219698,"title":"","content":"Well, personally, I dont feel like Promethean needs such a thing. If the concern is that the other splats gets more innate advantage by-way of these &quot;Aura Flares&quot;, then why not use this as an excuse to review the Promethean Condition itself and throw some more advantage after that?<br /> I see the state of being a Promethean as an inherently alien experience to all parties involved be it the Mage who wants to study the creature, the Mortal who fears the creature and the creature itself who just want to make friends (or whatever).<br /> My point is; giving them an Azoth-Flare as an inherent advantage implicitly hands the Promethean too much controle over their own unnatural condition. Many of the Prometheans innate benefits are 'Passive' in nature, and I very much like the narrative effect of this.<br /> It only adds to the fact, that I am generally not in favor of taking something from one system and slapping it onto another, for the express purpose of having it be &quot;That Supernatural thing that all the splats have!&quot;.<br /> <br /> If the other splats are getting more innate benefits, great! I am all in favor of having a discussion on what new innate benefits for the Prometheans might be. But I feel that an Azoth-Flare is the wrong direction to take on this. Sorry if this feels like a &quot;YOUR IDEA IS BAD!!11one!1!&quot;. I mean no offense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T22:45:56-07:00","id":219880,"title":"","content":"No offense taken. Brainstorming isn't about judgment.<br /> <br /> The notion isn't to give them parity with other splats, it's to explore how that design space might improve Promethean (not Promethean<i>s</i>). In Blood &amp; Smoke, Predatory Aura gives the Beast teeth and claws, and cements vampire attributes of seduction and violence. It gives players a tool that transforms the old Predator's Taint from a dangerous inconvenience to a game of dominance and a means of brute manipulation. It immerses the player into the vampire's way of thinking, which is fun. Better yet, it takes ideas that were reserved for Disciplines and makes them part of the Kindred condition, meaning that even the stuffiest Ventrue is as vicious and voracious as the most feral Gangrel. <br /> <br /> Prometheans don't need extra advantages. A Frankenstein can rip a werewolf in half, and a Centimani can awaken a horde of monsters out of rubble. All of them get a freebie death, if a power outlet doesn't make the point moot. Daybreak and thunderstorms and making friends and napping gives them their fuel stat. The question is, is the Azothic Radiance a candidate for a lashing aura treatment, and what should that look like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T23:00:22-07:00","id":219904,"title":"","content":"I feel it's worth pointing out that in rereading the corebook recently one of the things that sunk in for me was that not only are Prometheans corpse-robots, they're corpse-robots <i><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Animal_magnetism\" target=\"_blank\">powered by animal magnetism.</a></i><br /> <br /> The miasmatic qualities of the Disquiet seem more likely to act as the basis for an aura mechanic than Azothic radiance in general, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T23:13:53-07:00","id":219913,"title":"","content":"I have had the wrongest notion about animal magnetism all my life.<br /> <br /> Disquiet was always my first go-to, but given its contagion and overall negative feedback, why would a Promethean ever invoke it, save spite?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T23:26:54-07:00","id":219920,"title":"","content":"I can think of a number of reasons; but they\u2019re all covered by Disquietism Transmutations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T23:30:16-07:00","id":219921,"title":"","content":"Or Mesmerism; worth noting that the category's explicit use of the Disquieting aura is likely the reason Alembic penalizes attempts to affect its user with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T00:33:06-07:00","id":219945,"title":"","content":"Right. This is why I suggest tying it to Transmutation-neutral effects.<br /> <br /> I have this picture in my head of an angry Promethean drawing sparks and arcs from nearby metal, causing flames to rage and electronics to short out, as he approaches the intended victim of his wrath. Better yet, I see two Prometheans, meeting at a crossroads, and taking Measure through the forces at play, the black smoke of Torment choking the scene, as they both try to decide whether this fellow traveler is a threat or an opportunity. All of their Disfigurements are on display, there's no pretense, and they wrest the elements from both affronted Nature and jealous Divinity.<br /> <br /> Hmm, this sounds more like Demonic Form or even Going Loud. Radiance is the heat of the Azoth, which itself is a purified (purifying?) ember of the Divine Flame. It awakens the unliving Pandorans, it's tied to the potency of the Promethean's gifts, and it's the key component of Redemption. When it burns hot, it should be divine, elemental, vital, and transformative. The gods should fear it, because the Promethean is the ultimate usurpation of their powers by Man. Nature should fear it, because the Promethean represents the supreme violation of the natural order. Mortals definitely fear it, for here is something abandoned by the gods, contrary to every known law of life and death, and carries the keys to unlocking the entirety of human potential, but is a base, idiot mockery of themselves.<br /> <br /> More thinking out loud. I'll let you Brits do as you will while I sleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T10:50:35-07:00","id":220333,"title":"","content":"I would love Promethean to have a &quot;going loud&quot; mechanic. A point in the story where the promethean basically goes FU on his target and sheds his mask to reveal himself, feeling empowered by the azoth that's normally used to fuel his human shape. Even if this shape can only be attained in torment (so as to prevent the &quot;combat = go loud&quot; scenario).<br /> <br /> Aside from bonuses to physical stats (something like Frenzy from B&amp;S) I can think of only a few possible extra things, like automatically increase the wasteland, place the spooked condition on all mortal onlookers, doubling bonuses from Superhuman Potential, etc...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T10:48:26-07:00","id":226102,"title":"","content":"The idea I am working with in my games is that Prometheans can &quot;bleed&quot; Disquiet off - through their Radiance - to increase the Wasteland; basically, they can mark a place instead of inflict Disquiet.<br /> <br /> I'm sort of torn; on one hand, I think it would be nice to give Prometheans neat &quot;powers&quot; they can tap through their Azothic Radiance. On the other hand, all the Transmutations that work around/through Disquiet and the Wasteland already kind of do that, and I think it's more In-Theme if they can instead mitigate or shift around the downsides of their condition through their Azothic Radiance.<br /> <br /> You won't wake up any Pandorans for a scene if you Mark this area.<br /> You won't inflict Disquiet this scene if you Mark this area.<br /> You can't worsen Wastelands this scene, but everyone who succumbs to Disquiet goes to Stage 2 automatically.<br /> Your Azothic Radiance is doubled for the range at which Pandorans wake, but you won't inflict Disquiet or Wasteland.<br /> These are over-simplifications, maybe.<br /> <br /> I'm also greatly, greatly opposed to splat parity - on a certain level things should look the same, yes, but just as Harmony is different from Humanity is different from Cover, I don't think every Aura should give the same basic thing (in this case, cool powers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}